# Cursor rules — this repository

**Scope:** These rules apply to **this workspace** (the folder that contains `.cursor/rules/`). They are not global to your machine.

## Read project context first

At the start of **every** new conversation, read these in order:

1. **`.cursor/skills/task-management-workflow/SKILL.md`** — Full task workflow (proposals, to-dos, summaries, updates, testing). **Read this file in full every time**, not only when the user mentions tasks.
2. **`IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`** — Phases and status
3. **`structure/latest.md`** — Project layout and file roles
4. **`progress/latest.md`** — Active and completed tasks
5. **`task_summary/YYYYMM/YYYYMMDD/[most_recent].md`** — When continuing work

**`README.md`** (repo root) — Optional if present.

All detailed procedures for tasks, checklists, and “update” / “update all” live in **step 1** above — do not rely on copies in other repos or external projects.

## Folder organization (quick reference)

```
conversation_cursor/YYYYMM/YYYYMMDD/task_name.md
to-do/YYYYMM/YYYYMMDD/task_name.md
task_summary/YYYYMM/YYYYMMDD/task_name.md
progress/latest.md
structure/latest.md
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
```

## Other rules and skills in this repo

- **`agent-permissions.mdc`** — Web search and read-only git without prior chat approval; **`git commit`** and **`git push`** only after explicit user confirmation. Details: **`.cursor/skills/agent-permissions/SKILL.md`**
- **`.cursor/skills/python/SKILL.md`** — Python layout, Poetry **`poetry run`**, in-project **`.venv`** (read when editing or running Python).
- **`.cursor/skills/README.md`** — How optional skills are organized
